\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{The two first-loop observables}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{In the \vocabk{one-vertex Hurwitz model}{fdip-00ZA},
the \newvocab{first-loop trace} is the
\vocabk{Polyakov trace}{fdip-00X4}
##{\trace_F L_U.}
The trace is on the rank-#{4} coefficient fiber and is
not divided by its rank.}

\p{Let #{\psi_0=\pr_0\psi} and
#{\bar\psi_0=\bar\psi\iota_0}, using the independent
paired fields and degree-zero maps of the
\vocabk{dressed pair}{fdip-00WD}. The
\newvocab{first-loop dressed pair} is
##{P(U,V)=\bar\psi_0(L_U\psi_0).}
It uses the positively oriented first loop and identity
insertion #{M=\bbI_F}. The barred coefficient is
multiplied first. Its operator on the full cochain
space is #{\iota_0 L_U\pr_0}.}

\p{Write #{\Phi_m} for the
\vocabk{coupled finite coefficient functional}{fdip-00TU}
of this model. Its normalized values are
#{\langle\trace_F L_U\rangle_m=\Phi_m(\trace_F L_U)/Z(m)} and
#{\langle P\rangle_m=\Phi_m(P)/Z(m)} when
#{Z(m)\ne0}. The same normalization at one fixed
connection divides its paired coefficient by
#{\det K_{U,V}(m)} only when that determinant is nonzero.}
